# mcp-github-api — environment variables
#
# HOW THESE ARE LOADED. This server reads os.environ directly and does NOT load
# a .env file — there is no python-dotenv dependency and no load_dotenv() call
# in the repo. An MCP server receives its environment from the MCP client, so
# these belong in the client config: for Claude Code, ~/.claude/settings.json
# under mcpServers -> github-api -> env. Copying this file to .env has no effect.
#
# Authoritative reference: README.md "Environment Variables".

# GITHUB_TOKEN — required. GitHub personal access token with `repo` scope.
# Create at: Settings > Developer settings > Personal access tokens.
GITHUB_TOKEN=your_value_here

# GITHUB_REPO — NOT IMPLEMENTED. This file previously listed it as an optional
# "default repo in owner/repo format", but no code reads it: every tool takes
# the repository explicitly. Kept commented rather than deleted so the intent
# stays visible; README.md's table has always documented GITHUB_TOKEN alone,
# and it was correct.
# GITHUB_REPO=owner/repo
